# Product Intent (End User: Alyssa)

Fitness instructor (Zumba, Pound, etc.) across multiple organizations (mainly city rec). **Non-technical** end user: UI must stay simple, consistent, and **responsive on PC and mobile**. Goal is saving time vs manual spreadsheets — not spreadsheet-admin complexity.

## Must Support

- Students with contact info (email, phone, Facebook URL) **and** emergency contact
- Multi-class / multi-org attendance; ordered waitlists; drop/stop attending
- Contact waitlist or others to fill spots when absences are known
- Group/filter people by class; email current attendees of a class
- Session transitions (next session may change time/date/location or not run)
- “Create a new Session for this class” as a first-class flow
- Sign-in sheets as **Google Sheets**: scheduled people, columns per meeting date, attendance check-off, space for walk-ins, planned absences; easy to spot chronic misses
- Copy-friendly reports for pasting into email (see reports rule)

App replaces manual Google Docs spreadsheets. Sign-in sheet generation is the intentional spreadsheet exception.
